# Input graph for LA3D__cogitarelink-solid__tests_test_interop_foundation.py__test_registry_chain_covers_all_apps_every_registration_a_container_tree.
#
# The region asserts a chain of invariants and RAISES if any fails (bare
# `assert`, no graceful path), so the only call this driver can make is one
# where every invariant already holds (see meta.json/translation_notes for
# why the zero-solution branch cannot be exercised through run_pair here,
# same limitation as the sibling region of this batch). What the fixture
# DOES exercise:
#
#   * the full chain OWNER -hasRegistrySet-> hasDataRegistry-> 12
#     hasDataRegistration objects -- SEVERAL solutions for the one true
#     `m{ }` (not `.first()`) read in this region, `list(m{ {dreg}
#     interop:hasDataRegistration ?r })`;
#   * 7 "wiki" registrations whose registeredShapeTree starts with TREE_NS
#     and 5 named ones (registry:contacts-person/-organization/-group/
#     -membership, registry:id-schemes) with the exact ContainerTree IRIs
#     the region compares against;
#   * NEIGHBOURHOOD that must NOT match: a second owner (ex:otherOwner)
#     with its own registry set, and a second data registry
#     (ex:otherDreg) with its own registration (registry:decoy) that is
#     reachable only from that other registry, never from `dreg` -- if
#     `{dreg} interop:hasDataRegistration ?r` were scoped wrong (e.g. no
#     subject restriction), `len(regs) == 12` would fail loudly, since
#     registry:decoy would make 13.
@prefix interop: <http://www.w3.org/ns/solid/interop#> .
@prefix registry: <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/meta/interop/registry#> .
@prefix wiki: <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/meta/shapetrees/wiki-memory.tree#> .
@prefix ab: <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/meta/shapetrees/addressbook.tree#> .
@prefix idt: <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/meta/shapetrees/id-schemes.tree#> .

<https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/profile/card#me> interop:hasRegistrySet <urn:ex:rset1> .
<urn:ex:rset1> interop:hasDataRegistry <urn:ex:dreg1> .

<urn:ex:dreg1> interop:hasDataRegistration
    registry:concepts, registry:people, registry:places, registry:events,
    registry:organizations, registry:procedures, registry:working,
    registry:contacts-person, registry:contacts-organization,
    registry:contacts-group, registry:contacts-membership,
    registry:id-schemes .

registry:concepts       interop:registeredShapeTree wiki:ConceptsContainerTree .
registry:people         interop:registeredShapeTree wiki:PeopleContainerTree .
registry:places         interop:registeredShapeTree wiki:PlacesContainerTree .
registry:events         interop:registeredShapeTree wiki:EventsContainerTree .
registry:organizations  interop:registeredShapeTree wiki:OrganizationsContainerTree .
registry:procedures     interop:registeredShapeTree wiki:ProceduresContainerTree .
registry:working        interop:registeredShapeTree wiki:WorkingContainerTree .

registry:contacts-person       interop:registeredShapeTree ab:PersonContainerTree .
registry:contacts-organization interop:registeredShapeTree ab:OrganizationContainerTree .
registry:contacts-group        interop:registeredShapeTree ab:GroupContainerTree .
registry:contacts-membership   interop:registeredShapeTree ab:MembershipContainerTree .
registry:id-schemes            interop:registeredShapeTree idt:SchemeRecordContainerTree .

# Neighbourhood -- must not match: a second owner/registry-set/data-registry
# chain, entirely disjoint from the one under test, with its own
# registration that must not leak into `regs` (12, exact) or `wiki` (7,
# exact).
<urn:ex:otherOwner> interop:hasRegistrySet <urn:ex:otherRset> .
<urn:ex:otherRset> interop:hasDataRegistry <urn:ex:otherDreg> .
<urn:ex:otherDreg> interop:hasDataRegistration registry:decoy .
registry:decoy interop:registeredShapeTree wiki:DecoyContainerTree .
